#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:74
msgid "Integrating DAEs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:85
msgid ""
"In PyBaMM, a model is solved by calling a solver with solve. This sets up "
"the model to be solved, and then calls the method ``_integrate``, which is "
"specific to each solver. We begin by setting up and discretising a model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# Create model\n"
"model = pybamm.BaseModel()\n"
"u = pybamm.Variable(\"u\")\n"
"v = pybamm.Variable(\"v\")\n"
"model.rhs = {u: -v}  # du/dt = -v\n"
"model.algebraic = {v: 2 * u - v}  # 2*v = u\n"
"model.initial_conditions = {u: 1, v: 2}\n"
"model.variables = {\"u\": u, \"v\": v}\n"
"\n"
"# Discretise using default discretisation\n"
"disc = pybamm.Discretisation()\n"
"disc.process_model(model);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:117
msgid ""
"Now the model can be solved by calling ``solver.solve`` with a specific time "
"vector at which to evaluate the solution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# Solve #################################\n"
"t_eval = [0, 2]\n"
"dae_solver = pybamm.IDAKLUSolver()\n"
"solution = dae_solver.solve(model, t_eval)\n"
"#########################################\n"
"\n"
"# Extract u and v\n"
"t_sol = solution.t\n"
"u = solution[\"u\"]\n"
"v = solution[\"v\"]\n"
"\n"
"# Plot\n"
"t_fine = np.linspace(0, t_eval[-1], 1000)\n"
"\n"
"fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4))\n"
"ax1.plot(t_fine, np.exp(-2 * t_fine), t_sol, u(t_sol), \"o\")\n"
"ax1.set_xlabel(\"t\")\n"
"ax1.legend([\"exp(-2*t)\", \"u\"], loc=\"best\")\n"
"\n"
"ax2.plot(t_fine, 2 * np.exp(-2 * t_fine), t_sol, v(t_sol), \"o\")\n"
"ax2.set_xlabel(\"t\")\n"
"ax2.legend([\"2*exp(-2*t)\", \"v\"], loc=\"best\")\n"
"\n"
"plt.tight_layout()\n"
"plt.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/dae-solver.ipynb:170
msgid ""
"Note that, where possible, the solver makes use of the mass matrix and "
"jacobian for the model. However, the discretisation or solver will have "
"created the mass matrix and jacobian algorithmically, using the expression "
"tree, so we do not need to calculate and input these manually."
msgstr ""

